"text": "If a pie chart's printed percentage labels are treated as the authoritative market-share values, then the brand whose printed percentage is numerically greatest is the current market leader, and the corresponding public option should be selected.",
"component": "encoding/task relation",
"conditions": "Assumes the printed percentage inscriptions are valid and that 'current market leader' means the largest printed share."
},
{
"id": "r2",
"text": "If the pie chart's visible slice areas are treated as the authoritative market-share values, then the brand whose slice occupies the largest visible area is the current market leader, and the corresponding public option should be selected.",
"component": "encoding/task relation",
"conditions": "Assumes the drawn slice geometry is valid and that 'current market leader' means the largest visible slice."
},
{
"id": "r3",
"text": "If the printed percentage labels and the visible slice areas conflict, the chart is internally inconsistent, and the current market leader is underdetermined until the conflict is resolved.",
"component": "scale comparability",
"conditions": "Applies when the largest printed percentage and the largest visible slice belong to different brands."
}
